      "file": "src/mat5.c",
      "function": "Mat_VarReadNextInfo5",
      "line": 4828,
      "code": "",
      "note": "After InflateVarTag succeeds and uncomp_buf[0] == MAT_T_MATRIX, compressed variable parsing proceeds to array flags and rank/dimensions.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/mat5.c",
      "function": "Mat_VarReadNextInfo5",
      "line": 4857,
      "code": "bytesread += InflateRankDims(mat,matvar,uncomp_buf,sizeof(uncomp_buf),&dims);",
      "note": "InflateRankDims decompresses attacker-controlled compressed data from the MAT file into the stack buffer uncomp_buf. The decompressed tag at uncomp_buf[0..1] holds the dimensions byte count, which is the vulnerability-relevant tainted value. If the zlib stream ends or errors during tag inflation, InflateRankDims returns early without allocating a heap dims buffer, leaving *dims NULL.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/mat5.c",
      "function": "Mat_VarReadNextInfo5",
      "line": null,
      "code": "matvar->rank = nbytes / 4;",
      "note": "The dimension rank is derived from the attacker-controlled decompressed byte count without validating that it fits within the stack buffer capacity when dims aliases uncomp_buf+2. The fix adds: if (0 == do_clean && matvar->rank > 13) { error; break; }.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/mat5.c",
      "function": "Mat_VarReadNextInfo5",
      "line": 4870,
      "code": "matvar->rank = nbytes / 4;",
      "note": "The dimension rank is derived from the attacker-controlled decompressed byte count without validating that it fits within the stack buffer capacity when dims aliases uncomp_buf+2. The fix adds: if (0 == do_clean && matvar->rank > 13) { error; break; }.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/mat5.c",
      "function": "Mat_VarReadNextInfo5",
      "line": null,
      "code": "matvar->dims[j] = dims[j];",
      "note": "The copy loop reads dims[j] where dims aliases uncomp_buf+2. When j+2 >= 16 (rank > 13), dims[j] reads past the 16-element uncomp_buf stack array boundary, causing a 4-byte stack-buffer-overflow READ.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/mat5.c",
      "function": "Mat_VarReadNextInfo5",
      "line": 4877,
